;; Home-layer subagent overrides, symlinked to ~/.agents/subagents by the dotfiles
;; `agents.nix`. This is the middle link of the config chain:
;;   packaged skills/herdr-orch/subagents/config.edn
;;     <- this file (~/.agents/subagents/config.edn)
;;       <- project <git-root>/.agents/subagents/config.edn
;;
;; `merge-config` is `merge-with merge`, so a `:harnesses` entry here REPLACES the
;; packaged entry for that kind wholesale rather than merging its keys. Every entry
;; below must therefore restate `:model-flag`; omitting it fails validation at parse
;; with this file's path.
;;
;; WHY: Claude Code and Codex both default to interactive per-command approval, so a
;; spawned subagent stalls at its first tool call waiting for a human who is not
;; watching its pane. The parent then reports a timeout while the child sits blocked.
;; These flags make non-interactive delegation possible for those two harnesses.
;;
;; RISK: this grants every claude- and codex-kind subagent unsandboxed, unprompted
;; command execution in the caller's worktree, for every project on this machine.
;; That is a deliberate trade for a single-user workstation; do not copy it onto a
;; shared or internet-exposed host. `pi` is intentionally omitted -- it is not
;; affected by this class of approval stall, and granting a bypass it does not need
;; would widen the blast radius for nothing.
;;
;; Verified: Claude Code 2.1.220 (`--permission-mode` choices include
;; `bypassPermissions`), codex-cli 0.145.0
;; (`--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`).

{:harnesses {:claude {:model-flag "--model"
                      :extra-args ["--permission-mode" "bypassPermissions"]}
             :codex  {:model-flag "--model"
                      :extra-args ["--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox"]}}}
